A1. Name something that makes a good slipper. ~ PEEL
A5. What is the most excellent, funniest magazine in the world? The first letter is J and the last is E. (Any little boy or girl getting the right answer can receive JUDGE for 1 year by sending it in accompanied by a $5 bill to JUDGE, 627 W. 43rd St., New York City.—Adv.) ~ JUDGE
A8. What impels most girls to dress as they do? ~ MALE
A12. What do workmen do when the boss is around? ~ LABOUR
A14. What is a word which means colloquially "caught with the goods"? ~ NAILED
A16. Who makes used cars? ~ USERS
A17. Name something that's always odd. ~ ONE
A19. What is difficult for the man to do when in double harness? ~ DRIVE
A20. What is a Scotch word which means to entrap, ensnare? ~ GIRN
A21. Name something it is difficult for most people to face. ~ FACTS
A23. Name a word which means level; smooth. ~ EVEN
A24. Name a suffix which is often used to form a plural. ~ ES
A25. What is the first thing any baseball player would like to make? ~ BASEHIT
A27. What suffix is used to form the comparative degree? ~ ER
A28. Name a conjunction which marks an alternative. ~ OR
A29. What is the name of a fairy or elf in Persian mythology? ~ PERI
A30. What does any man do who turns his salary over to his wife? ~ ERRS
A32. What does a "yes" man say in Spain? ~ SI
A34. What causes great embarrassment when they part? ~ SEAMS
A35. Name something which is an asset for any boxer to have. ~ REACH
A37. What did the Volstead Act fail to make the U. S.? ~ DRIER
A38. What did Red Grange make at college—and since? ~ GAINS
A39. What do vacationists take for ennui? ~ TRIPS
A42. What do anti-prohibitionists desire to put down? ~ BEERS
A44. Who was the Egyptian sun god? ~ RA
A46. What is a cutting thing to do? ~ SNIP
A47. What did Paul Revere do to become famous? ~ RODE
A48. What is the symbol for tellurium? ~ TE
A49. What is the motto of the "go-getter"? ~ DO
A51. In what country are people especially intent on making their marks in the world? ~ GERMANY
A53. Name a very personal pronoun. ~ ME
A54. What is a pain-in-the-neck? ~ SORE
A56. What are election days in Ireland? ~ RIOTS
A57. At what events is much broadcasting done? ~ TEAS
A59. What are all Scotchmen who pay income tax? ~ ANGRY
A61. Give a nickname for a man whose name is the same as one of the months of the year. ~ GUS
A62. What does the young daughter do for a new hat? ~ TEASE
A63. What is a flop? ~ FIASCO
A65. Name something often found stewed. ~ OYSTER
A66. Give the name of an Anglo-Saxon hireling or serf. ~ ESNE
A67. What is a way to keep a flapper's affection? ~ SPEND
A68. Give the name of an ancient maritime city of Phœnicia. ~ TYRE

D1. Name one thing that can stop liquor from flowing. ~ PLUG
D2. How would you feel if you had $1,000,000? ~ EASIER
D3. What German novelist was also an Egyptologist? ~ EBERS
D4. Name a synonym for "forsaken." ~ LORN
D5. Who is the author of "Here's How"? (abbr.) ~ JR
D6. Give another name for dumb-belle. ~ DUNCE
D7. What is half an "em"? ~ EN
D8. What should all autoists steer clear of? ~ MIRE
D9. What can no "dead-one" be? ~ ALIVE
D10. What does any motorist need if he decides to shift for himself? ~ LEVERS
D11. Name a garden famous for its apples. ~ EDEN
D13. What country could be called "the land of the spree"? (init.). ~ US
D15. What is it that editors never reject? ~ AD
D17. What is a speak-easy? ~ OASIS
D18. What could be used as a ticket to Dreamland? ~ ETHER
D21. Where do people who know their onions live? ~ FARM
D22. What name of respect is given usually to elderly men? ~ SIRE
D25. What must a young society climber have to get on? ~ BEARING
D26. What is it to marry more than once? ~ TRAGEDY
D28. What does a salesman get for his money? ~ ORDER
D29. What are some big guns called in England? ~ PEERS
D31. What do evil spirits do? ~ SCARE
D33. What noun means "to pass out"? ~ ISSUE
D34. What do most Congressmen do in Congress? ~ SIT
D36. Name a masculine possessive pronoun. ~ HIS
D40. What is a good thing for an old tar to tie up to? ~ PIER
D41. What is another name for a small shoot or twig? ~ SPRIG
D42. What are the kids next door? ~ BRATS
D43. How long does it seem since prohibition was passed? ~ EONS
D45. Who was the youth Venus fell in love with? ~ ADONIS
D48. What is another name for a "goat-getter ?" ~ TEASER
D50. What musical instrument do you have to give the air before you get the air? ~ ORGAN
D52. What little quadruped has made many a belle hop? ~ MOUSE
D53. What should good meat pie be? ~ MEATY
D54. At what place are blow-outs often held? ~ SAFE
D55. What is the language of the Gaels or Celts in the Highlands of Scotland? ~ ERSE
D57. What is the hardest thing for a speeding college boy to pass? ~ TEST
D58. Name an adjective which means brown, or dry. ~ SERE
D60. Give two of the four initials of a famous man's organization? ~ YC
D62. Who is famous for his base thefts? (Nickname.) ~ TY
D64. Give a Latin word meaning bone. ~ OS
D65. What kind of uniform did the A. E. F. wear in the World War? (init.). ~ OD


